================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
================================================================================

This template bundles patches/scripts that build on the following projects.
None of these projects' source code or compiled binaries are included in this
repository — they are downloaded or installed at build time on the user's
machine. Nonetheless, their licenses are listed here for transparency.

--- 1. NativePHP Mobile ----------------------------------------------------
URL:      https://github.com/NativePHP/mobile-air
License:  MIT License
Version:  3.2.2 (v3 series, "NativePHP Air")
Use:      Composer dependency (`nativephp/mobile`), downloaded at
          `composer install` time into `vendor/`. Not redistributed here.
Note:     The patch `patches/laravel-environment-mysql.patch` in this
          repository is a diff against a Kotlin file generated by NativePHP.
          The patch itself is tiny and distributed under the same MIT terms.

--- 2. v3l0c1r4pt0r/php-ndk ------------------------------------------------
URL:      https://github.com/v3l0c1r4pt0r/php-ndk
License:  MIT License
Use:      The `mobile-libphp-builder/` directory is derived from this
          project. The original Dockerfile, Makefile, and patches
          (`fork.patch`, `resolv.patch`, `ext-standard-dns.c.patch`,
          `ext-standard-php_fopen_wrapper.c.patch`,
          `main-streams-cast.c.patch`) were copied and then modified for
          NativePHP Mobile + MySQL compatibility.

--- 3. Laravel Framework ---------------------------------------------------
URL:      https://laravel.com/
License:  MIT License
Version:  13.x (installed via `composer create-project laravel/laravel`)
Use:      Application framework, downloaded via Composer. Not redistributed.

--- 4. PHP ----------------------------------------------------------------
URL:      https://www.php.net/
License:  The PHP License, version 3.01
          https://www.php.net/license/3_01.txt
Version:  8.3.30 (downloaded by `mobile-libphp-builder` at build time)
Use:      Runtime compiled for Android. Modified via patches in
          `mobile-libphp-builder/*.patch`. The name "PHP" is a trademark
          and may not be used to endorse or promote derived products.

--- 5. OpenSSL ------------------------------------------------------------
URL:      https://www.openssl.org/
License:  Apache License 2.0 (OpenSSL 3.x series)
Version:  3.0.15 (downloaded by `mobile-libphp-builder` at build time)
Use:      Cryptography library, cross-compiled for Android arm64.

--- 6. Oniguruma ----------------------------------------------------------
URL:      https://github.com/kkos/oniguruma
License:  BSD 2-Clause License
Version:  6.9.9 (downloaded by `mobile-libphp-builder` at build time)
Use:      Regex engine used by PHP's mbstring extension.

--- 7. libxml2 ------------------------------------------------------------
URL:      https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2
License:  MIT License
Version:  2.12.7 (downloaded by `mobile-libphp-builder` at build time)
Use:      XML library used by PHP's dom/simplexml/xml* extensions.

--- 8. SQLite -------------------------------------------------------------
URL:      https://www.sqlite.org/
License:  Public Domain
Version:  3.47.2 (amalgamation, downloaded at build time)
Use:      Optional local database engine.

--- 9. Android NDK -------------------------------------------------------
URL:      https://developer.android.com/ndk
License:  Android Software Development Kit License Agreement
          (Google Inc.)
Version:  r27c (downloaded in Docker build stage)
Use:      C/C++ cross-compilation toolchain for Android.

--- 10. MySQL Community Server -------------------------------------------
URL:      https://www.mysql.com/
License:  GNU General Public License v2.0 (Community Edition)
Version:  8.4 (Docker image `mysql:8.4`)
Use:      External database server, run as a separate Docker process.
Note:     This template does NOT link against or embed MySQL source code.
          Communication is via the MySQL client/server protocol (TCP/IP)
          using `mysqlnd` (a pure-PHP driver bundled in PHP itself, under
          the PHP License). No GPL obligations are triggered.

================================================================================
DOWNSTREAM DISTRIBUTION NOTICE (for users who ship APK/IPA)
================================================================================

If you use this template to build and distribute an Android APK or iOS IPA
that contains the compiled PHP runtime (`libphp_wrapper.so` / embedded
`libphp.a`), please be aware that the final binary will contain code from
multiple third-party libraries (OpenSSL, Oniguruma, libxml2, SQLite, PHP,
etc.), some of which are licensed under LGPL or other licenses that impose
redistribution obligations:

1. **GNU libiconv** (LGPL 2.1) — bundled by NativePHP's distributed
   `libphp.a`/`libiconv.a`. When redistributing the resulting binary, you
   must either (a) provide source/object files so that end users can relink
   with a modified libiconv, or (b) dynamically link libiconv. Consult a
   lawyer if in doubt.

2. **OpenSSL** (Apache 2.0) — attribution required in "NOTICES".

3. **PHP** (PHP License) — the name "PHP" cannot be used to endorse derived
   products.

4. **MySQL** (GPL, if bundled) — this template does NOT bundle MySQL;
   only connects to an external MySQL server. No GPL obligation arises
   from this template alone, but check your final deployment.

**YOU**, the distributor of your APK/IPA, are responsible for complying
with all applicable third-party licenses, not the authors of this template.
The authors provide NO warranty regarding license compliance for downstream
uses.
